{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Who has counted the dust of Jacob</b> — He says: I see them from the peaks of the mountains dwelling alone, and I cannot count them, for they are alone like the dust of the earth, which no man can count. And also the fourth part of Israel in the four camps of the standards I cannot count. He prophesies concerning them that they shall multiply and not diminish, and they shall always be alone — the seed of Jacob like the sand of the sea, which cannot be measured or counted. And this is the view of Onkelos (Onkelos on Numbers 23:10) regarding רֹבַע יִשְׂרָאֵל. It is also correct that it should be like \"my path and my lying down You have measured\" (Psalms 139:3), from \"you shall not sow your field with two kinds of seed\" (Leviticus 19:19) — that is, רֹבַע in the sense of sowing/lying down — as in the expression \"and from the waters of Judah came forth\" (Isaiah 48:1). And he said: <b>Let my soul die the death of the upright, and let my end be like his</b>, to say that they inherit the Garden of Eden, for the end of man is death; therefore he asks that he die the death of the upright — they are Israel, who are called Jeshurun — that they spend their days in goodness, and let my end be like his, like Israel, whose portion is in life and who are not children of Gehinnom and Abaddon. Behold, the general thrust of his prophecy this time is that HaShem does not desire their curse, and that we are a people apart, His portion and His people, not intermingled among the nations and not reckoned with them, and our end is good on the straight path."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:13.238922669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}